{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790346889,"nonce":"vfD5CqrdxPVF4lC2xlMwkCIDlds=","title":"zyntax compile's LLVM AOT output skips the LLVM optimisation pipeline","message":"compile_llvm (crates/zyntax_cli/src/backends/llvm_aot.rs) builds a bare LLVMBackend and writes the object file straight from the unoptimised module: no IR pass pipeline runs, and the TargetMachine is created for the \"generic\" CPU. The JIT tier's LLVMJitBackend already runs the pass pipeline and picks the host CPU; the AOT path should reuse that setup (with an explicit target CPU for cross builds). No test drives `zyntax compile`, so a test that compiles and runs an AOT binary is owed with the fix.","files":null}]}